    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In the curves above, starting with the precision/recall curve, the precision stays roughly the same because the model is unable to accurately make predictions given the data available. For that reason, precision stays the same no matter what direction the threshold is moved. However, the recall drops as the threshold is increased naturally because fewer and fewer values fit the threshold.\n",
        "\n",
        "Recall should be prioritized over precision when having a few false positives is not detrimental to the desired outcome, for example when conducting research for a paper and seeing some sources that are irrelevant. Precision should be prioritized when a false positive could be detrimental, like when identifying fraudulent bank transactions especially for large amounts."
      ],
